name: Custom.Atlas.WinAuthFailures
description: |
  Atlas-managed (Windows): stream failed logons from Security Event ID 4625 via
  watch_evtx, emitting the target account and source network address. Feeds the
  Python-side Behavior.AuthBurst rule (N failures per source IP within a window
  → password spray / brute force).

  Requires the "Audit Logon" failure auditing policy (on by default for member
  servers/DCs; may need enabling on workstations). No Sysmon dependency.

type: CLIENT_EVENT

parameters:
  - name: SecurityChannel
    description: Windows Security event-log channel.
    default: Security

sources:
  - query: |
      SELECT
        System.TimeCreated.SystemTime AS timestamp_utc,
        EventData.TargetUserName AS user,
        EventData.IpAddress AS source_ip,
        EventData.WorkstationName AS workstation,
        EventData.LogonType AS logon_type
      FROM watch_evtx(filename=SecurityChannel, accessor="event_log")
      WHERE System.EventID.Value = 4625
        AND source_ip != "" AND source_ip != "-"
